# ── git here is for the CODE, and the RUNTIME assets that make it run. ─────────
# Source art (.glb sculpts, hundreds of megabytes) stays out: it is binary,
# effectively static, does not need per-line history, and makes every git
# command crawl. Back it up separately (a drive or a cloud folder).
#
# 2026-07-18: assets/ and the game's sound ARE tracked. They were ignored once, so a
# GitHub zip download arrived with no models and no sound and the game could not run.
# The runtime set is fine for git; the .glb source art stays OUT — 369 MB in 9 files,
# and palm_tree.glb alone is 233 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, which
# would make the push fail outright.
#
# 2026-07-24: the site was FLATTENED (website/* moved to the repo root, engine.html
# renamed index.html). The old rule was a bare `/sound/` — under the old layout that
# ignored the root-level source audio while website/sound/ stayed tracked. Flattening
# merged those into ONE sound/ folder, so `/sound/` would now exclude sound/sfx/ —
# the only audio the game actually loads — and reintroduce the silent-game bug above.
# Hence: exclude the unused music libraries BY NAME, and keep sound/sfx/ tracked.

# ── unused audio libraries (646 MB) — verified zero references in index.html ──
# The game loads ONLY sound/sfx/*. These are the composing/source library and must
# not ship: they bloat the repo and risk GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
sound/classical/
sound/anthem/
sound/soundtrack/
sound/8bit/
sound/life/
sound/environment/

# ── source art trees — not loaded by the game ──
art/
.vox/
website_old/
_snapshots/

# .glb sculpts are the source form; the game loads baked .vox instead
*.glb

# scratch
*.bak
*.log
node_modules/
